## 7. Exact computation and validation boundary

The standard-library verifier reconstructs (2), checks reflection, checks equality
with the canonical five-block partition when `r=1`, and uses exact arithmetic in
`Q(sqrt(3))` to check every original nearest-neighbor constraint with a moved
endpoint. It also checks within-block contacts. Run:

```text
python3 research/kuperberg_alternating_strip_exact.py
```

Its finite cases are independent bookkeeping checks. The table and inequalities
prove all `n,r,d` in Theorem 1. The non-neighbor bound and the recursive collar
argument are human proofs, not outputs of finite enumeration. The script does not
certify global optimality, arbitrary-source embedding, or promotion.

Verified output in this run: **96 exact strip endpoints, 24 exact path samples,
357,434 nearest-neighbor constraints; all passed.** The theorem-state checker and
`git diff --check` also passed. Regenerating the artifact index additionally supplied
missing default-unreviewed metadata headers for 28 pre-existing reports from the
starting commit; those metadata-only changes promote no claim and alter no proof.

## 8. Exact remaining obligation and promotion boundary

The new free-gap architecture gives (8), and (12) supplies a stronger restricted
capacity theorem. The next source-level obligation is precise:

> In a surviving Target A source branch, extract a primitive-direction aligned gap
> of width `d_D` together with its full uniformly phased moving/insertion region,
> unblocked by any exterior source point, with available radius `R_D` satisfying
> `d_D^(-1) log(1/d_D)=o(log R_D)`; carry the final add-one set in a container of
> diameter strictly below the source diameter or convert it into the exact Schur
> deficiency.

Neither contact-forest dimension nor positive strain alone proves this quantitative
and exterior-compatible extraction. The Schur sector surplus remains open. A source
with an arbitrarily small gap or an exterior-blocked patch is not eliminated by this
report.

**Promotion recommendation:** preserve as an unreviewed research packet and obtain
an independent proof/collar audit. A promotion of (8) must update the manifest,
Target A route and active prompt, relevant Section 157/160 frontier language,
generated state views, and the registered certificate in one transaction. The
canonical five-block results remain valid and should remain available as the fixed
architecture benchmark.
